  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows sustained negative sentiment (e.g., multiple -0.25 or 0.00 values), indicating market pessimism.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent price spikes — if true outcome exceeds model forecast by >5% after a spike, adjust next forecast upward to avoid underestimating momentum.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if model consistently overpredicts prices in early periods (e.g., first 5-7 days of history), reduce forecast by 1-2% per day to align with observed mean reversion.",
    "When sentiment shifts from neutral to positive (e.g., 0.00 → 0.50 or 0.67), increase forecast by 1-3% to reflect bullish momentum.",
    "Avoid over-optimism in late-period forecasts — if model forecasts are consistently >10% above true outcome after day 15, reduce forecast by 2-5% to prevent overestimation of future price.",
    "If sentiment history includes a 0.67 followed by 0.00, assume market correction is imminent — reduce forecast by 3-5% to account for potential reversal."
  ]
